 The total normal vector $d\Sigma_\mu$ for an N-cycle is calculated as the sum of the individual triangle normal vectors $d\sigma^i_\mu$, associated with the average point of the N-cycle [S1, unofficial].
 
+**Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
+*   **Corner Contact:** VESTA does not connect voxels that share only a single common point (corner contact) by default, as their VFVs never meet, resulting in two separate surfaces [S1, unofficial]. Forcing this connectivity requires inserting a tubular template, which is not standard [S1, unofficial].
+*   **POA Consistency:** A consistent global or local selection must be made for all POAs to prevent tearing/holes in the final surface [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Redundancy:** Original VESTA produces the minimum required support points, whereas template-based methods like MCA generate significantly more redundant support points [S1, unofficial].
+
